comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-26T04:54:49.262Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete strict all-status corpus plus live request-specific searches and full terminal-lineage reads found no exact active owner. Existing SDK promotion and transaction/preview delivery remain completed; this item owns the newly requested public surface."
  "2026-10-28T19:44:07.695Z","harness:codex","Implementation scope: retain original item plans in coordinator journals, expose read-only status and host-bound guarded abandonment/supersession, refuse committed and peer-edited work, preserve append-only compensation and audit evidence. Complete strict 3148-item all-status census has no omissions; 38 open GitHub issues each already have a canonical PM link comment. No open PRs or GitHub dependency/code/secret alerts at intake."
  "2026-10-28T20:16:18.094Z","harness:codex","Native late-peer recovery oracle initially exposed a delete-store gap: the existing scoped item precondition was checked by update/close but not by locked deletion. Isolated candidate adds the same assertion before deletion policy/hooks and centralizes create compensation ownership checks. Close and delete both preserve a peer edit injected immediately before item-lock acquisition. Isolated focused proof passes51 tests; original checkout remains frozen for the in-flight full coverage run. Retirement intent is additionally retained before compensation to fence forward replay across recovery crashes."
  "2026-10-28T20:39:10.736Z","harness:codex","Validation: linked recovery suite passed 65/65, including durable v2 retirement fencing, prepared/applied/recorded crash boundaries, interrupted compensation, audit deduplication, malformed/downgraded receipts and native peer-write races. Typecheck, ESLint, duplicate detection, registry audit and OSV passed. Full canonical coverage is running; no full-coverage success is claimed yet. First complete suite exposed contract snapshot/source-operation registration and preview clock comparison failures, now corrected; its npm package resolution failure was host NODE_PATH configuration, now explicitly set. Published 2026.10.28 verifier passed npm/npx/Bun/bunx and GitHub release checks; this does not imply publication of these branch changes."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-28T20:16:19.379Z","harness:codex","Retiring an interrupted batch requires a durable intent before compensation, not only a terminal status afterward. Every destructive compensation must recheck ownership under the target item lock; a pre-lock history comparison alone does not protect a late peer edit."
